Z||000002||Oreif||04-15-2000||01:20 AM||||Radio Shack sells a 5 1/4 long throw woofer that replaces the factory woofer and sound 10 times better! I've replace a few of them in friends cars. The woofer is sold as a single speaker for $15.99! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||04-15-2000||10:40 AM||||Ya know.....Just how much bass can you get out of a 5 1/4" woofer???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I wonder if you can stuff a 8" into that stock box??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-15-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000004||Oreif||04-15-2000||12:19 PM||||An 8" won't fit but a 6 1/2" Boston Acoustic or MTX free-air sub will fit wit a little "creative" trimming!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>If you go to a bigger woofer I would upgrade the amp. The stock 12 watts RMS amp won't drive the bigger woofers efficently.||||reg||1
